WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:06.080
While 2017 is far from over, the year has
already been stacked with surprising on-screen

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:07.080
deaths.

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:11.050
From fan favorites to characters who some
wish had been given the ax ages ago, here

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:14.830
are some of the most surprising small screen
killings of the year so far.

00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:18.359
And as always, beware the huge spoilers ahead.

00:00:18.359 --> 00:00:19.359
Jane the Virgin

00:00:19.359 --> 00:00:24.960
At the end of Jane the Virgin's second season,
Michael Cordero, Jr. was shockingly shot in

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:29.550
his hallway, but the beginning of Season 3
offered fans a collective sigh of relief when

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:32.040
they learned he'd managed to survive his injuries.

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:36.469
But... halfway through the season he died
of a related heart condition anyway.

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:40.539
Michael's death itself wasn't too much of
a shock, since the narrator told viewers he

00:00:40.539 --> 00:00:45.430
would love Jane "until he drew his dying breath,"
but when he survived the shooting, it seemed

00:00:45.430 --> 00:00:48.980
like he'd at least stick around for the rest
of the season.

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:50.719
Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:00:50.719 --> 00:00:52.640
During Season 4 of Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:57.739
Dr. Radcliffe spent much of his time escaping
the pain of real life within the virtual reality

00:00:57.739 --> 00:00:59.430
Framework he created.

00:00:59.430 --> 00:01:04.320
The episode "Self Control" finally gave fans
a good look inside his realm of computerized

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:08.680
consciousness, but when evil android Aida
learns that his intentions for the Framework

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:13.220
might not be what she thought, she slashes
his wrists, forcing him to stay there.

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:15.400
"This is the way the world ends.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:17.540
Not with a bang but a ... "

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:21.640
Will he come back from death, Coulson-style?

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:22.880
Maybe.

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:25.970
But few fans saw this abrupt twist coming.

00:01:25.970 --> 00:01:27.140
The Vampire Diaries

00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:33.259
Fans of The Vampire Diaries were foaming at
the mouth when Enzo St. John's heart was unceremoniously

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:35.880
ripped out near the end of the show's final
season.

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:40.689
Sure, his murderer, Stefan Salvatore, was
in Ripper mode and wasn't his whole self again

00:01:40.689 --> 00:01:45.340
until after Bonnie injected him with the cure,
but killing a gal's forever love when things

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:48.729
were just starting to get good between them
was especially raw.

00:01:48.729 --> 00:01:53.729
Stefan ultimately made up for it by sacrificing
himself so another couple, Damon and Elena,

00:01:53.729 --> 00:01:55.390
could have their happily ever after.

00:01:55.390 --> 00:01:59.880
But the only thing that made this even remotely
bearable was the fact that Enzo got to come

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:04.890
back in ghost form and hang out with Bonnie
even after his untimely passing.

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:06.570
Big Little Lies

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:11.010
Readers of Liane Moriarty's novel of the same
name might not have been surprised by Perry

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:15.570
Wright's brutal end in Big Little Lies, but
for those who watched HBO's adaptation of

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:17.970
the story, his passing was a shocker.

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:22.870
In the very first episode of the show, a death
was teased, but it wasn't until the end that

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:24.650
fans found out who would meet their maker.

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:29.450
Perry was abusive to his wife, was in the
process of passing on his most terrible tendencies

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:34.760
to his son, and committed sexual violence
against town newcomer Jane some years before,

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:38.530
so he definitely deserved what was coming
to him, but still.

00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:39.530
Yowza.

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:40.750
The Walking Dead

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:45.420
There's no shortage of death on The Walking
Dead, but the show's seventh season was filled

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:47.780
with some especially shocking deaths.

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:51.541
But thanks to the magic of the Internet and
awareness of the comics upon which the show

00:02:51.541 --> 00:02:56.210
is based, the brutal demises of Abraham and
Glenn weren't altogether unforeseeable.

00:02:56.210 --> 00:03:01.150
However, when Sasha decided to take a suicide
pill while stuffed in a coffin before Negan's

00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:05.770
dramatic showdown, he was quite surprised
to find her emerge from the box as an infected

00:03:05.770 --> 00:03:10.000
walker who wanted nothing more than to take
a bite out of his bat-wielding arm.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:11.000
"Sash.

00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:17.500
You're not gonna believe this crap… holy
god damn!"

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:21.680
That sacrifice proved to be of little use
to the survivors, since it was one of Negan's

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:24.980
lackeys who took the brunt of her brutality,
but still.

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:26.610
Brave girl.

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:27.620
Homeland

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:32.690
Peter Quinn endured a lot of life-threatening
things on Homeland, including a stroke, getting

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:34.840
gassed, and a struggle with alcoholism.

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:39.260
Ultimately, however, he gave up his life for
his country, putting himself in the line of

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:43.110
fire to save President-elect Keane and get
her to the White House.

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:47.270
Now, fans might have to learn to love a new
assassin-turned-hero.

00:03:47.270 --> 00:03:48.270
The Leftovers

00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:54.700
HBO's always fascinating The Leftovers started
its third and final season with a literal

00:03:54.700 --> 00:04:00.090
bang when Meg Abbott blew the Guilty Remnant
to smithereens, taking young convert Evie

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:01.090
Murphy with her.

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:05.060
Since viewers had already believed Evie was
dead once before, her death didn't come as

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:09.050
much of a shock as Meg's; many fans figured
she'd last through the end of the series.

00:04:09.050 --> 00:04:13.370
Maybe it's most shocking that the Guilty Remnant
are gone—and Meg was the cause.

00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:15.720
"Well, that's not gonna work."

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:17.680
Prison Break: Resurrection

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:22.580
The revival of Prison Break, appropriately
titled Prison Break: Resurrection revived

00:04:22.580 --> 00:04:27.550
the show with much of the original cast intact—only
to kill off one fan favorite in the fourth

00:04:27.550 --> 00:04:28.550
episode.

00:04:28.550 --> 00:04:32.180
Though Paul Kellerman was thought to be dead
in Season 2, viewers later learned it was

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:36.580
a cover-up; when the show returned, Kellerman
was a changed man who'd hung up his gun and

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:38.190
was living a righteous life.

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:42.060
Unfortunately, you can't put your past behind
you—which was a lesson driven home when

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:43.990
Kellerman was killed by an assassin.

00:04:43.990 --> 00:04:44.990
Arrow

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:48.210
Over the course of five seasons of Archer,
Malcolm Merlyn the Magician was alternately

00:04:48.210 --> 00:04:53.099
a force of pain and justice, and his end came
in the form of noble sacrifice.

00:04:53.099 --> 00:04:58.000
On the run from Adrian Chase on Lian Yu, Thea
stepped on a landmine, and Malcolm, who'd

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:02.360
come to the island to protect his daughter,
took her place on top of the mine, allowing

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:03.810
her to run to safety.

00:05:03.810 --> 00:05:08.310
Left to confront Chase's minions, Malcolm
took his foot off the landmine, wiping them

00:05:08.310 --> 00:05:10.990
out—and giving up his own life in the process.

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:12.330
Empire

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:17.120
The members of the Lyon family often act irrationally
and destructively, which is what provides

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:20.199
the soap opera theatrics that make Empire
so fun.

00:05:20.199 --> 00:05:23.439
Perhaps there's nobody in the series quite
as unhinged as Leah.

00:05:23.439 --> 00:05:27.610
She's also never been fond of Tariq, the illegitimate
child of the family.

00:05:27.610 --> 00:05:32.219
Tariq was just about to tell his half-brother
Lucious about a kidnapping plot, but Leah

00:05:32.219 --> 00:05:34.800
put a stop to that with a fatal stab to the
neck.

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:39.249
It's a death that was surprising, bloody,
and sad because Lucious and Tariq were just

00:05:39.249 --> 00:05:42.189
beginning to treat each other like brothers.

00:05:42.189 --> 00:05:43.189
Fargo

00:05:43.189 --> 00:05:47.979
To many viewers of the third season of FX's
Midwestern crime anthology, it seemed like

00:05:47.979 --> 00:05:51.879
Nikki Swango would be the last person standing
when all was said and done.

00:05:51.879 --> 00:05:55.889
After all, the petty criminal pulled the strings
from the beginning, orchestrating the plot

00:05:55.889 --> 00:06:01.050
to extort money from her parole officer fiancé's
wealthy twin brother…and then always rolling

00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:05.770
with the punches, staying a step or two ahead
of both the police and the bad guys when plans

00:06:05.770 --> 00:06:06.770
went sour.

00:06:06.770 --> 00:06:11.430
But even though the crafty Nikki survived
countless brushes with death, she still somehow

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:16.840
met an unceremonious end when she was shot
by a police officer during a roadside standoff.

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:21.249
All these devastating demises just go to show
that when it comes to small screen drama,

00:06:21.249 --> 00:06:23.229
no one's safe from an early exit.

00:06:23.229 --> 00:06:24.229
Thanks for watching!

00:06:24.229 --> 00:06:27.150
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:29.229
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

